    {
      "id": "ladder",
      "title": "It only moves one way",
      "body": "So the work climbs. A request becomes a written spec, then drawings, then something you can click, then real code — and every step is cheap to be wrong at compared to the one after it. It only moves one way. The rules only ever get stricter as they pass down, never looser, and nothing gets to skip a step because it feels confident.",
